ast-v8-to-istanbul 1.0.6 -> 1.0.6-project.1

Upstream: https://registry.npmjs.org/ast-v8-to-istanbul/-/ast-v8-to-istanbul-1.0.6.tgz
(MIT, Ari Perkkio). Applied by scripts/build-coverage-producer.mjs with exact
context; the same file, reverse-applied, must give back the upstream bytes.

dist/index.mjs: the walker marks every nested LogicalExpression of a chain as
"skipped" so that only the outermost node registers the binary-expr branch.
On entry, a skipped node was also treated as an ignored subtree, which
stopped traversal of everything under it: a callback inside the left operand
of `a && b && c`, its body statements and its branches were never
registered, and a consumer then scored that body from the enclosing
function alone. The nested node keeps its branch-deduplication skip, which
the LogicalExpression case honours by returning early, but no longer becomes
an ignore boundary, so its descendants are walked like any other expression.
Ignore hints (`v8 ignore next|if|else`) are matched before this check and
keep their subtree semantics.

package.json: version 1.0.6-project.1, so the installed package names the
repair.

